                <pb facs="0259" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg179"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Prince Chi’ng.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness</hi>: A recent telegram from Chentu
                    indicates that the state of affairs there is still serious.</p>
                <p>I must therefore urge the Chinese Government to take prompt measures to restore
                    order in the disturbed district.</p>
                <p>I embrace, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
